<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14707" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŏmĭtrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		domitor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>she who tames</i> or <i>subdues</i>
			(very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equorum Epidaurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 44</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">FERARVM DOMITRICEM DIANAM,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1447</span></i>
			; and <b>poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferarum clava (Herculis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					9, 117</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum omnium (ferrum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 16, 25, § 127</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
